ly we benefit football fans  benefit because it gives us something  in this wasteland of groundhog day that  that we hope or at least we know is  going to be there in some form or  fashion  mike i think i do think it's it's a  cliche you know i live in new york and i  watch a lot of these andrew cuomo  sessions on television every morning he  goes on for about an hour and i watch  him and he basically  has said in 48 different ways  we are going to come out of this as  stronger people  and i totally agree with him these  hardships that we're not used to dealing  with i mean some people have real  hardships and some people are dying and  so i think we all have to consider  that  damn it we are lucky to live in this  country i am i am i am  i'm so i'm so proud when i look i'm  walking my dog in brooklyn new york and  i pass by 30 people and they're all  wearing masks and they all when you come  when you're going to pass somebody on a  sidewalk  they go as far as they can to one side i  go as far as i can it's just simply  being considerate  and this is not going to last forever  but as long as it lasts  i got to tell you i'm um what i've seen  in my world you know i'm proud of people  and i think we're going to come out of  this  uh being proud of each other whenever  all is said and done  well said peter and we'll end it on that  note we'll be back on thursday with  another edition of pro football talk  live check out the peter king podcast  wherever podcasts are available for the  larry zonka interview football morning  in america still plenty of stuff in  there if you haven't read it yet this  week new one coming on monday new pft  live tomorrow we'll talk to everybody  soon have a safe and happy wednesday  we'll see you  [Music]  thursday hi i'm mike tarico and thanks  for watching make sure to hit subscribe  for the latest news and highlights from  nbc sports
 

